-- title:
--   Formally smooth centred subalgebra at a non-supersingular smooth centre, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\hat\jmath$ denotes the element of the base-changed modular function field given by the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant, and $C$ denotes the chart algebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ ↥F₀ ⟨_, hjF₀⟩`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), i.e. the $A₀$-subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over the $A₀$-subalgebra generated by $\hat\jmath$.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $q$, subject to the hypothesis `hq3` that $q = 3$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ which lies over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), namely $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, which by `hW` consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (those places that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value on the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$); and the inclusion `hle` of the base-changed full modular function field $\overline F_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of level $M'$ into the geometric level field $\overline F =$ `fieldBar q M'` attached to $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** A `ConstantReduction` structure $R_0$ for $A$ with source $\overline F_{M'}$ and target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\overline F_{M'}$, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, compatibility of the residue with $A$ on constants, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a constant scaling into the integers with nonzero residue, and compatibility of `placeMap` with divisors of elements of nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\overline F_{M'}$ defines an element of `R₀.integers` whose $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Uniformiser and root of unity.** An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπ`) and $\pi \in A$ (`hπP`), and an element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   **Igusa valuation rings.** A family $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\overline F$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, subject to four hypotheses: `hIg_inf` identifies $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, at the point `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$, as the set of $f$ whose Laurent expansion can be written as a quotient of coefficientwise images of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of nonzero reduction; `hIg` provides, for each $\ell$, an element $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction mod $q$ carries $[1:0]$ to $\ell$ and for which $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of the family; and `hIg_perm` asserts that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   **Supersingular (Drinfeld) valuation rings.** A family $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}$ of valuation subrings of $\overline F$ indexed by $W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ precisely when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of $\overline F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ has non-negative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\overline F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference between the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$; `hSS_fix`, that each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **Descent data.** A subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ over which $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is algebraic, with $\pi \in K_0$ (`hπK₀`); a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ together with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ (`hι`, `IsLocalHom`) whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`); a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ (`hϖ₀π`); a subfield $F_0 \subseteq \overline F$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image of $\hat\jmath$ (`hjF₀`), with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ compatible with $\iota$ (`hj₀`), and with $\hat\jmath \neq 0$.
--
--   **The valuation ring, its centre, and the chart.** A valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V$ contained in the Igusa ring at infinity (`hV`: every $f \in V$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$) and properly so (`hVlt`: some $f \in F_0$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ but does not lie in $V$); the containment `hCV` of the chart algebra $C$ in $V$; a maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $C$ (`h𝔫max`) which by `h𝔫` is the centre of $V$ on $C$, i.e. $g \in \mathfrak n$ iff $g$ lies in the nonunits of $V$; the hypothesis `hnotSS` that $\mathfrak n$ is not a supersingular centre, namely for each $s \in W$ some $g \in C$ has image in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ yet $g \notin \mathfrak n$.
--
--   **Igusa components on the chart, and generic fibre.** A family $\mathfrak q$ of ideals of $C$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with: `hLOC`, that for each $\ell$ an element $x \in F_0$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ precisely when $x = b/c$ with $b, c \in C$ and $c \notin \mathfrak q(\ell)$; `hMIN`, that each $\mathfrak q(\ell)$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; `hINJ`, injectivity of $\mathfrak q$; and `hSURJ`, that every minimal prime over that ideal is some $\mathfrak q(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hGENFIB` states that for every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ not containing the image of $\varpi_0$ there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ consisting exactly of the fractions $b/c$ with $b, c \in C$ and $c \notin \mathfrak p$.
--
--   **Smoothness input.** An open subscheme $U$ of the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₀ ↥F₀ ⟨_, hjF₀⟩`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two Spec maps attached to the finite and infinite chart algebras) containing the image of the point $\mathfrak n$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ under the canonical morphism `ιFin` (`hxU`), such that the open immersion `U.ι` followed by the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ is smooth (`hU`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$ such that all of the following hold. (1) $B$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra. (2) $B$ is integrally closed in $F_0$: every $x \in F_0$ integral over $B$ lies in $B$. (3) $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $B$: every $x \in F_0$ satisfies $xc = b$ for some $b, c \in B$ with $c \neq 0$. (4) Every prime ideal of $B$ which contains the extension of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and is not maximal is a minimal prime over that extension. (5) For every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ not containing the extension of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ consisting exactly of the fractions $b/c$ with $b, c \in B$, $c \notin \mathfrak p$. (6) If all of $B$ maps into $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell')$ then $\ell' =$ `lineInfty q`. (7) For no $s \in W$ does all of $B$ map into $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$. (8) There is a prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ such that $x \in F_0$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ precisely when $x = b/c$ with $b, c \in B$, $c \notin \mathfrak q$. (9) Every minimal prime $\mathfrak q$ over the extension of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ has this same property: $x$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ iff $x = b/c$ with $b, c \in B$, $c \notin \mathfrak q$. (10) $B$ is contained in $V$. (11) $\mathfrak m$ is the centre of $V$ on $B$: $b \in \mathfrak m$ iff $b$ lies in the nonunits of $V$. (12) Either $\hat\jmath \in B$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1} \in B$. (13) The structure map from $A_0$ to the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$ is formally smooth.
--
--   This is the affirmative branch of the Igusa-chart dichotomy for semistable models of modular curves at the prime $q = 3$: at a centre lying on the finite $\hat\jmath$-chart which is not a supersingular centre and which admits a smooth open neighbourhood in the descended two-chart model over $A_0$, a finitely generated, integrally closed $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ centred at $V$ is produced whose special fibre sees only the Igusa component at infinity and no supersingular ring, and whose localisation at the centre is formally smooth over $A_0$. It is the $q = 3$ counterpart of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$, and it is consumed by the dichotomy statement that either such a package exists or all elements of the relevant ring lie in the nonunits.
